---
description: Ask before changing any existing test; new tests are fine
alwaysApply: true
---

# Existing tests need permission

Do not edit, rewrite, delete, or weaken a test that already exists in the repo unless the user has explicitly allowed that change in this conversation.

That includes assertions, fixtures, helpers, parametrization, skips/xfails, names, and imports inside an existing test file.

```text
# BAD — agent changes an existing test to match new code
# (no user yes)

# GOOD — ask first, wait for yes, then edit
# "This would change test_quote_night in test_list_price_quote.py. OK to update it?"
```

Allowed without asking:

- Creating a **new** test file
- Adding a **new** test function in a **new** file

Adding a new test function to an existing file still counts as modifying that file — ask first.

If the user said to implement a feature or fix a bug, that is not permission to change existing tests. Ask, then wait.
